# BUILT 9 Oct 2026 (eng, third pass) — difficulty filter is server-side

The Difficulty dropdown used to hide cards on the **current page only**. Now it filters **every** competition: the list sends `?difficulty=` to `GET /api/competitions`, and `browseCompetitions` turns it into an `_id $in` clause on the normal query. That means pagination, totals, sort and the featured KPIs all count only the matching competitions.

- Difficulty is **derived** from eight fields and is never stored, so the server scans the candidate competitions (same visibility and filters, projected to `DIFFICULTY_SOURCE_FIELDS`), works out each one's difficulty in JS, and keeps the matching ids. A warning is logged if more than 5,000 are scanned.
- There is **one definition** of difficulty: `difficultyForCompetition` in `lib/competitions/competition-difficulty-input.ts`. Both the label on each card and the server filter call it, so a card can never be labelled with a difficulty its filter disagrees with. It imports no database model, so client components can use it (R58).
- An unknown `difficulty` value is ignored (checked against a `Set`), not treated as "match nothing".
- Platform leverage comes from `getTradingRiskSettings()`, falling back to 100, the same value the client uses.
- Join GM still only opens the lobby. That is correct and was deliberately not changed.

